<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US midterms: 'Donald Trump's wings have been more than clipped'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e7ce1e013d3d8612f057dcf57a613ff98a732799d3a2b58fc40886c33cb6598</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:46:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-donald-trump-s-wings-have-been-more-than-clipped" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump faced a radically transformed and hostile political landscape after Democrats seized both the House of Representatives and the Senate in Tuesday's (November 3) midterms. The result was a personal humiliation for the 80-year-old Trump, leaving him as a lame duck president for the remaining two years of his term. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Identity crisis': Can Democrats 'deliver' following their 'historic', once in a generation victory?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35c630b39aba4b52f4b3990ae256ccb7a1f5fd84b9bf8cbd1637a3c1ebb15514</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:27:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/identity-crisis-can-democrats-deliver-following-their-historic-once-in-a-generation-victory" /><summary type="html">A historic Democratic electoral breakthrough has transformed the American political landscape. For Laurie Dundon, Senior Associate Fellow at the European Leadership Network and former US diplomat, the central question is whether the Democratic Party can convert electoral momentum into coherent governance. "Can they deliver?" Dunden examines the apparent disintegration of Donald Trump's 2024 MAGA coalition alongside the Democratic Party's continuing ideological struggle between its progressive and centrist wings. Ahead of 2028, Dunden cautions against seeing Trump as a lame duck: "Trump is never going to stop being Trump." The resulting struggle over congressional spending powers, presidential vetoes, tariffs and investigations promises to be a delicate dance to watch".</summary></entry><entry><title>Bent on leaving his mark: Trump's proposed 'Triumphal Arch' sparks backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:286a35ec510951df14199e492120fcc36f42cb7936d11256cd62341e7f5ab2f5</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:55:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261105-bent-on-leaving-his-mark-trump-s-proposed-triumphal-arch-sparks-backlash" /><summary type="html">Since his return to power, US President Donald Trump has been intent on reshaping the nation's capital Washington, seeking to leave his name and mark on it. After his involvement with the Kennedy Center, the White House ballroom and the Lincoln Memorial Reflecting Pool, Trump is now particularly keen on building a 250-foot (79-metre) "Triumphal Arch" – a project he claims is intended to honour the 250th anniversary of the United States.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>What comes next for Democrats after midterm election victory?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f1a057badafaeccc5e98029e6951073a4feb5baab22e04b3476fc6fc8f8e071</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:54:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-what-comes-next-for-democrats-after-midterm-election-victory" /><summary type="html">With the US midterms over, Democrats are turning to what could become one of their most crowded and unpredictable presidential primaries in decades – a 2028 contest ​likely to expose the party's divide over how to win back the White House. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Farewell Botox, heels and big hair: Is this the end of MAGA women?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c60f5d8e322964793e5812495b16fe255b62774cce473a9d280a5b3bab966b26</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:15:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261105-farewell-botox-heels-and-big-hair-is-this-the-end-of-maga-women" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, November 5: "Loser" and "Reborn in the USA" are just some of the headlines dominating the international press after the Democrats stomped to victory in the US midterm elections. What impact will their success have on the rest of Donald Trump's presidency? How will he govern with a Democratic-controlled Congress? These are just some of the burning questions after that vote. Also, do the midterm results signal the end of the MAGA woman and the "Mar-a-Lago face"?</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Elon Musk fails $440 million bet as Republicans lose</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd76ac96186cf3e45ba1860d85efe33638235101a29ed4d48fa826168c372f84</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:29:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-elon-musk-fails-440-million-bet-as-republicans-lose" /><summary type="html">The 2026 midterm elections were the most expensive on record, with nearly 12 billion dollars spent during the campaign. Tech tycoon Elon Musk was by far the largest individual donor ever, injecting over 440 million dollars of his money to support the GOP. Tuesday's resounding Democratic victory showed the limits of his money, power and influence.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Democrats say ready to negotiate and promise big changes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e26f8f1c8ca61e0dc7f29ff3e1105416017bf679ab1c16541429e6611e73b6f</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:22:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-democrats-say-ready-to-negotiate-and-promise-big-changes" /><summary type="html">US Democrats are promising to leverage their landslide election win to bring down living costs and hold President Donald Trump's administration to account. They are set to take control of both chambers of Congress in January, but delivering on their agenda could mean striking deals with the very president they have pledged to rein in.</summary></entry><entry><title>Melania Trump to host Ukrainian, Russian officials at White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88ea86213eb94114e0806b743aa8fd26832530a65676db45d1014b0b488a7886</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T05:23:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-melania-trump-to-host-ukrainian-russian-officials-at-white-house--000b54c4acdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-melania-trump-to-host-ukrainian-russian-officials-at-white-house" /><summary type="html">Russian and Ukrainian officials, including human rights chiefs, are set to meet US First Lady Melania Trump at the White House Thursday ahead of Abu Dhabi talks aimed at ending the Ukraine war. It comes weeks after Melania Trump helped broker a partial ceasefire enabling the evacuation of civilians from the Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's second-term playbook: Fake news, AI and attacks on his critics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88234da33f38a21c67bf10c653694df3da9d28dafa283938316ff7a288de5abc</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:44:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261104-trump-s-second-term-playbook-fake-news-ai-and-attacks-on-his-critics--e29038ea0d3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261104-trump-s-second-term-playbook-fake-news-ai-and-attacks-on-his-critics" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump could be credited with popularising the term "fake news", but his own presidency has been riddled with numerous false claims, conspiracy theories and misleading content. In this special fact-checking segment, Vedika Bahl examines Trump's second term: his consistent attacks on political opponents, use of AI-generated images to glorify himself and push political narratives, and what happens when journalists challenge him.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Blue wave across America: Do US midterms signal beginning of the end for Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c05160392973d947556dc302d5528927abe525f566093812154715fbdd03123a</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T19:49:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261104-blue-wave-across-america-do-us-midterms-signal-beginning-of-the-end-for-trump--f1d9ca650a12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261104-blue-wave-across-america-do-us-midterms-signal-beginning-of-the-end-for-trump" /><summary type="html">He asked people to pretend he was on the ballot and they did. Voters across the United States have chased US President Donald Trump's Republican majorities from both houses of Congress. How big a landslide is this for the Democrats?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Democrats warn Trump camp to ‘lawyer up’ as anger over corruption drives midterms wipeout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b6cb0f0e2ee332a29e9600d6a66a391a634833425b6ad792ab2096d2357d37b</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T18:01:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-democrats-warn-trump-camp-lawyer-up-anger-over-corruption-drives-midterms-wipeout-gop--7b31d5ddc778.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-democrats-warn-trump-camp-lawyer-up-anger-over-corruption-drives-midterms-wipeout-gop" /><summary type="html">Corruption in government was high on the minds of US voters as they dealt US President Donald Trump’s party a chastening defeat in midterm elections, toppling Republican strongholds like dominoes and flipping both chambers of Congress. Triumphant Democrats have warned the Trump administration to “lawyer up”; how they go about tackling alleged graft and abuse of power could shape both their own fortunes and the country’s politics.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Once-in-a-generation event: Historic election a shocking repudiation of Trump &amp; the MAGA movement'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10893d80a1c0cc486484abe52eb78957863566aee2011642cfb4d728d6d7abe0</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:49:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/once-in-a-generation-event-historic-election-a-shocking-repudiation-of-trump-the-maga-movement--e99c6f8b95fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/once-in-a-generation-event-historic-election-a-shocking-repudiation-of-trump-the-maga-movement" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Adam Jentleson, President of the Searchlight Institute and author of Supermajority: How Democrats Can Build Lasting Power, For Jentleson, the Democrats' sweeping midterm victory represents far more than the familiar backlash against an incumbent president. "This is a once-in-a-generation event." But electoral breadth presents a governing dilemma. Can a coalition stretching from progressive reformers to culturally conservative Democrats translate its diversity into legislative action? "Pluralism is not just a political strategy. It is actually a moral good in a democracy," he insists. But electoral breadth presents a governing dilemma. Can a coalition stretching from progressive reformers to culturally conservative Democrats translate its diversity into legislative action? And can a party united by opposition to Trump sustain that unity when confronted with difficult choices over healthcare, immigration, economic inequality and climate change?</summary></entry><entry><title>European leaders welcome Democrats' US midterms election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32047be6f24ff1c62fc70ce658d799caa99c7aa90436fdb2dfa06eeb56c9a25e</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:00:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-welcome-democrats-us-midterms-election-win--9eb298186d7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-welcome-democrats-us-midterms-election-win" /><summary type="html">European leaders voiced hopes for a reset with the United States on Wednesday, November 4, after voters delivered a huge midterm election defeat to President Donald Trump and his Republican party. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms bring a wave of historic firsts as minorities win key races</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e063ae846495236a82443f7815d7a0e713169e32135256ccfb2c1f150f1d689</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:51:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-bring-a-wave-of-historic-firsts-as-minorities-win-key-races--466ff9f5f4fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-bring-a-wave-of-historic-firsts-as-minorities-win-key-races" /><summary type="html">US midterms bring a wave of historic firsts as minorities win key races: The first Native American female senator in Minnesota, the first openly gay male senator in New Hampshire, the first Muslim senator in Michigan and the country's first Black female governor in Georgia. FRANCE 24's Elitsa Gadeva has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Iran's deputy parliament speaker reacts to Trump's elections setback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81bf956ba48bf8b9e784d5955c51b75be8e1788300073b5189b56b078657c876</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:50:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-iran-s-deputy-parliament-speaker-reacts-to-trump-s-elections-setback-1--b3baa850b100.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-iran-s-deputy-parliament-speaker-reacts-to-trump-s-elections-setback-1" /><summary type="html">First Deputy Speaker of the Parliament of Iran Ali Nikzad on Wednesday attributed Republican losses in the US midterm elections to Washington's war with Iran, telling lawmakers that American efforts to pressure Tehran had failed.  Democrats won control of both chambers of Congress in Tuesday's midterm elections.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer on US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56c2dfe0af35d2edd855e8ef4933d5268d01128655dde853431ffccd3ec82c83</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:42:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-senate-democratic-leader-chuck-schumer-on-us-midterms--86de370c3725.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-senate-democratic-leader-chuck-schumer-on-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">The US Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer talked to the press after the midterm election results. Democrats are riding their sweep of Congress into a new era, eager to meet voter demands for change with plans to tackle high costs of living and confront President Donald Trump's final years in the White House.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: How will Trump manage working with Democrats?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ba71548039a32759daf13583c707cb92edfef8d8d65be66f7444893741d4489</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:24:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-how-will-trump-manage-working-with-democrats--595e74419046.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-how-will-trump-manage-working-with-democrats" /><summary type="html">Democrats are riding their sweep of Congress into a new era, eager to meet voter demands for change with plans to tackle high costs of living. How will Donald Trump manage to work with them? FRANCE 24's Ophelie Jacobson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tale of 2 midterms: Republican redistricting 'backfired' while Democrats 'exceeded all expectations'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8870578474599bbbc2f6737c7f26dac357cac76b8fa3579428d76078c12e6d3</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tale-of-2-midterms-republican-redistricting-backfired-while-democrats-exceeded-all-expectations--e3ed6aa1e437.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tale-of-2-midterms-republican-redistricting-backfired-while-democrats-exceeded-all-expectations" /><summary type="html">Following a resounding Midterm election defeat, Is MAGA Losing Its Grip on the Republican Party? Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Bryan Lanza, Republican strategist and Partner in Mercury's Washington DC office. "The big thing about MAGA was confrontation, in your face," explained Lanza. But following a veritable blue wave, he believes the electorate has delivered a warning: "We need to move beyond that." While Donald Trump has acknowledged the Democratic victory, at times combative, at times conciliatory, Lanza argues that the president must begin his final two years in office reversing damaging tariffs, addressing widespread dissatisfaction with immigration enforcement and navigating a highly unpopular Iran war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump after the midterms: Gridlock, impeachment and succession?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3110d9bbc71e8d101b687d2c2dc69dc6ae7c23c13c68a896ffe9cda770bbb30</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:54:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-trump-after-the-midterms-gridlock-impeachment-and-succession--6a13fd719356.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-trump-after-the-midterms-gridlock-impeachment-and-succession" /><summary type="html">Following the US midterms, US President Donald Trump could face a turbulent final two years in office. From budget battles to potential impeachment proceedings, what does the new political balance of power mean for his presidency? FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle breaks it down.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: 'Maybe the best colour for Texas is purple'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02e0326dd729be2e43c99fe4d2bc5f6c57b0127a4b7b03d1c9575672b3af33eb</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-maybe-the-best-colour-for-texas-is-purple--208d404b28e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-maybe-the-best-colour-for-texas-is-purple" /><summary type="html">Texas flipped blue following the US midterm elections, marking a historic shift for a state that hasn't been led by Democrats in decades. The legacy of prolonged Republican leadership has left a lasting mark, but as Democrat James Talarico said with this election, 'maybe the best colour for Texas is purple.' FRANCE 24's Texas correspondent Andres Espinal reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Is Republican Party able to pivot away from MAGA movement, or will it sputter forward leaderless?'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c18897ee2a2d4e6d27dd0f4483c762a2c499ef63f6ad59c26493704d0724ca91</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:16:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/is-republican-party-able-to-pivot-away-from-maga-movement-or-will-it-sputter-forward-leaderless--65a3a2fd5e2f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/is-republican-party-able-to-pivot-away-from-maga-movement-or-will-it-sputter-forward-leaderless" /><summary type="html">Does an electoral repudiation of Donald Trump also mark the beginning of MAGA’s decline? Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Ian Reifowitz, SUNY Distinguished Professor of Historical Studies at Empire State University, who describes the Republican defeat as “an absolute and complete repudiation” of the president. He connects voters’ economic frustrations with resentment over presidential enrichment, while questioning whether ideological differences between progressive and moderate Democrats proved decisive. Looking towards 2028, Reifowitz identifies a central Republican dilemma: “If JD Vance is the nominee, he can’t run against Donald Trump”, yet Trump himself may refuse to relinquish control of the party.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: Gen Z gives Democrats their strongest support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e51c191fe8f9cba6e4adc4190e69d20f47ff1a820cbfb65cb922a986645a08e</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:10:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterm-elections-gen-z-gives-democrats-their-strongest-support" /><summary type="html">In the US midterm elections, 50 million members of Gen Z were eligible to vote. Young voters gave Democrats the strongest support, with 75% of them voting for the party. This generation will be the biggest voting bloc in the United States in the coming years. FRANCE 24's Ophelie Jacobson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms: How Abdul El-Sayed used 'humour and hope' to rebuff racism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b7e994115daef6ddec3602fa9f998aff03cf62551c1e8b50325497cc99d819f</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T14:25:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-midterms-how-abdul-el-sayed-used-humour-and-hope-to-rebuff-racism" /><summary type="html">Abdul El-Sayed is set to become the first Muslim senator in US history following his midterms victory in Michigan. His victory came despite what he has denounced as racist attacks against him, inlcuding from Donald Trump, which, says FRANCE 24's correspondent Jessica Le Masurier, he rebuffed with a mixture of "humour and hope".</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: 'It is now going to be pretty chaotic for Donald Trump'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5a088a7c4635a64caf908b343a6f6f3343b8e4178586f40e168dac8e52621b1</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T14:12:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-it-is-now-going-to-be-pretty-chaotic-for-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">The Democrats' victory in the midterm elections have left Donald Trump in a difficult position for the rest of his mandate. The now "blue" House of Representatives will decide the budget, which Trump will have to accept and follow. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian's 'not expecting drastic change in US policy' after midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:faaeab17593490281f8756f044aca71c689b24c775d883d7acd38b9bbe779c59</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:26:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-s-not-expecting-drastic-change-in-us-policy-after-midterms--6a22a8195d02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-s-not-expecting-drastic-change-in-us-policy-after-midterms" /><summary type="html">Ukrainians do not expect the Democrats' victory in the US midterm elections is change much in regards to US policy on the war with Russia, or at least not quickly, says France 24's correspondent in Kyiv Emmanuelle Chaze. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky has not reacted yet to the "blue wave" taking control of Congress in the US.</summary></entry><entry><title>A look back at how Trump's political decisions saw his approval rating plummet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0f38132caa963fb79fc271bee69a9eaba51850b4f72b218cd10f239ed529ffc</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:17:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-a-look-back-at-how-trump-s-political-decisions-saw-his-approval-rating-plummet" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's unpopularity has been cited as a major factor in the Democrats' sweeping victory in the midterms. The latest polls show Trump's approval rating has plummeted to 37.3%, down from 42% in his first midterm election. What were the political decisions that led to such a dramatic decline?</summary></entry><entry><title>Blue wave sweeps across America: 'In 1974, we had Watergate babies, now we have Iran War babies'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4508f036237561b4b8fc6ba4dc619fb39feee6d506911b59f901f4d3812ddeb2</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:00:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/blue-wave-sweeps-across-america-in-1974-we-had-watergate-babies-now-we-have-iran-war-babies" /><summary type="html">Stuart Norval welcomes France 24 International Affairs Editor Philip Turle and Hind Ziane, Geopolitical analyst and founder / CEO of Genpo. "In 1974, we had the Watergate babies. Now we have the Iran War babies," remarks Ziane with this striking historical analogy. Just as the Watergate scandal helped propel a new generation of Democratic lawmakers into Congress in 1974, Zian argues that public disillusionment with the Iran war, mounting economic pressures and dissatisfaction with Donald Trump's leadership may now be reshaping the American political landscape. Yet Turle reminds us, "They're not voting for Democrats because they love the Democrats. They're voting for the Democrats because they don't like Donald Trump."</summary></entry><entry><title>What consequences for Israel as Democrats win the US midterm elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1f4c3cfa964b18569be0d3a046d1cb4c39644b7f326f67ea484c1ddbc2184d8</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:32:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-what-consequences-for-israel-as-democrats-win-the-us-midterm-elections--b88554bea6f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-what-consequences-for-israel-as-democrats-win-the-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Democrats seized control of the US Congress on Tuesday, capturing the Senate and House of Representatives in a stunning upset. What are the potential consequences for Israel and Benjamin Netanyahu, as Trump announced on Tuesday that the US will halt $3.8 billion in aid to the country? FRANCE 24's correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Trump reacts to the Democrats’ sweeping victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fe4439729c4b1f7145ec123b930bb54650d6df67312150ee120f400c133d64c</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:24:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-trump-reacts-to-the-democrats-sweeping-victory" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump had rare praise for rival Democrats Tuesday after their stunning US midterm elections victory and admitted the Iran war may have played a part in the defeat of his Republican Party. But the 80-year-old refused to take any personal responsibility for the result.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms bring surge of historic firsts for women and minorities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:226462df6cb78620119f4b8b6243664e24efe7cd9ff6bf2fb5b2ddedfb46927c</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:15:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-us-midterms-bring-surge-of-historic-firsts-women-members-minority-groups" /><summary type="html">The 2026 US midterm elections will go down in history for the Democrats' dramatic takeover of both houses of Congress but also for a surge of historic firsts for women, LGBT, Black and Native American candidates, as well as the election of the first Muslim US senator.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
